{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And these are the generations of Aaron and Moses.</b> It mentions only the sons of Aaron, yet they are called the generations of Moses — because he taught them Torah. This teaches that whoever teaches his fellow's son Torah, Scripture accounts it as though he begot him (Sanhedrin 19)." "<b>On the day YHWH spoke to Moses.</b> These became his generations — that he taught them what he had learned from the mouth of the Almighty."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :register {:flags {1 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:10.892776975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}